from dec_part1 import d
d("use-case-shopping/create_suggestions.py::filter", "a", "accepted", "C4.S2 — `len(text) < 3` already returned True on line 58, so `text.startswith(\"/\") and len(text) < 3` (line 60) can never be true; deleting it removes a startswith call per title that gets this far (report-only, one call per input)")
d("examples/google-cloud/cloud-functions/python/main.py::listfiles", "a", "accepted", "C4.S8 — `blob.name.__contains__(file_filter)` (line 46) spelled as a method call; `file_filter in blob.name` is the idiom with the operator's fast path. file_filter is checked for None above, so both forms do the same test")
d("examples/google-cloud/cloud-functions/python/main.py::getlogs", "a", "accepted", "C4.S8 — `blob.name.__contains__('.zst')`, `blob.name.__contains__(file_filter)` and `json_data['uri'].__contains__(uri_filter)` (lines 61, 63, 69) use the dunder spelling of `in`; both sides are str, so the operator gives the same answer")
d("reverse-image-search/script/feed.py::run", "a", "accepted", "C4.S7 — `ex[\"image\"]` and the isinstance check run before the cheap `abs_path.exists() and not refeed` skip (lines 136-140), so already-fed rows still pay for image access. The repair must not count non-image rows as skipped (the original does not count them), so the skip test goes first and the image test keeps its own branch")
d("text-search/python/collect_training_data.py::build_dataset", "a", "accepted", "C5.S1 — `int(qid) not in processed_queries` (line 75) tests membership in a list that load_processed_queries builds (lines 63, 67), once per query; a set built once answers each test in O(1). The list's len() is still used on line 72, so the repair keeps the list and adds a set beside it")
d("examples/embedder-auto-training-evaluation/training-evaluation/train.py::TrainDataset.__getitem__", "a", "accepted", "C5.S1 — pop(0) followed by append on query['positives'] and query['negatives'] (lines 27-33) rotates the list on every access; deque gives O(1) rotation. Only this method reads those lists, so the change stays inside the class (report: lists are short)")
d("news/src/python/evaluate.py::predictions", "a", "accepted", "C5.S2 — find_hit scans hits['root']['children'] linearly for each news_id (lines 64-65), n x m; one dict keyed by news_id, built once per call with first-occurrence semantics, answers each lookup. A missing id still raises TypeError on hit['relevance'] as before")
d("news/src/python/train_cold_start.py::read_bert_embeddings", "a", "accepted", "C5.S3 — `np.zeros([num_news, 512])` is float64 for a buffer that torch.FloatTensor then copies to float32; a float32 buffer holds the same rounded values at half the size and skips the copy")
d("news/src/python/convert_embeddings_to_vespa_format.py::read_embeddings", "b", "rejected", "`Looks like it, but is not`: the float32 rounding is part of the output, since the values are later printed with %.6f after the float32 conversion; removing the np.array conversion changes the printed digits")
d("news/src/python/create_bert_embeddings.py::create_embeddings", "e", "accepted", "C5.S4 — `outputs[0].tolist()[0][0]` (line 59) converts the whole (1, L, 512) hidden-state tensor to nested lists to keep the first token's 512 values; `outputs[0][0].tolist()` gives the same floats for the first token and converts only that row")
d("hypencoder/encode_query.py::main", "a", "rejected", "`Looks like it, but is not`: np.array(..., dtype=float32).tolist() turns the ids into float values after a float32 rounding, so removing the round trip changes the element type the model receives (ints) — output contract")
d("visual-retrieval-colpali/src/backend/vespa_app.py::VespaQueryClient.query_vespa_colpali", "a", "accepted", "C5.S4 — the query tensor goes tensor -> tolist() (format_q_embs) -> np.array -> packbits for the binary query; the sign bits could come from the tensor. Report-only: the float list is still needed for input.query(qt), so the saving is one array conversion per query, and the repair spans float_to_binary_embedding")
d("rag-blueprint/eval/train_lightgbm.py::perform_cross_validation", "b", "accepted", "C5.S4 — the model dict is dumped to a string, each feature name is regex-substituted across the whole JSON (one pass per feature), then re-parsed and dumped again; renaming the dict directly avoids the serialise/parse round trip")
d("visual-retrieval-colpali/src/main.py::full_image", "a", "rejected", "`Looks like it, but is not`: the file on disk must stay the JPEG bytes, so the base64 encode on a cache hit cannot be removed without keeping a second in-memory copy, which is a different design rather than this unit's repair")
